## Interface: 20506
## Title: |cFFFFD100ToonAge|r |cFF888780Anniversary|r
## Notes: TBC character advisor — stat caps, weapon skill, cap-aware gear scoring, racials and profession perks.
## Author: SIRC
## Version: 2.2.1-anniversary
## DefaultState: enabled
## SavedVariables: ToonAgeDB

# Interface 20506 confirmed against three addons already running on this client:
# ElvUI_TBC.toc, ZygorGuidesViewerClassicTBCAnniv.toc and DugisGuideViewerZ.toc.
#
# Scope: advisory only. No guide engine, no navigation, no arrow — the player
# uses Dugi for questing. See Docs/CLASSIC_ANNIVERSARY_BRIEF.md in the _ptr_ repo.
#
# ── FILENAME, RENAMED 2026-09-10 ────────────────────────────────────────
# This file used to be the unsuffixed ToonAge.toc. Renamed to the Blizzard-
# recognized "_TBC" suffix (Burning Crusade Classic & Anniversary Edition —
# verified against Warcraft Wiki's TOC format reference, not assumed) as the
# first step of the multi-TOC pattern: a future ToonAge_Cata.toc or
# ToonAge_Mainline.toc can now sit next to this one, each parsed ONLY by its
# matching client, without the two ever colliding. An unsuffixed ToonAge.toc
# is Blizzard's universal fallback name — since this one is now correctly
# suffixed, there is deliberately no generic ToonAge.toc left in this folder;
# having both would leave a second manifest around that isn't the one the
# client actually reads on this flavor, which is worse than removing it.
#
# IMPORTANT: this rename alone does NOT add Retail or Cataclysm/Mists Classic
# support. Every file below is still TBC-only game-design data (talent
# builds, hit/expertise caps, rotations) that would need its own research and
# its own Data/*.lua per additional flavor — see Core/Environment.lua's
# header comment for why that part can't be shimmed the way an API
# difference can.

# ── Core Framework ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Load order matters: Utils defines TA.Utils, which every later file binds at
# file scope. Init must precede it to create TA and TA:RegisterModule.
# Environment loads right after Init so every later file can read real
# WOW_PROJECT_ID-based flags (TA.IsTBC, TA.flavor, ...) instead of the
# hardcoded literals Init.lua used to set directly.
Core\Init.lua
Core\Environment.lua
Core\Utils.lua
Core\State.lua
Core\Layout.lua
Core\UI.lua
Core\MinimapButton.lua
Core\ApiGuard.lua

# ── Combat maths ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Core\TBCStats.lua
Core\SkillScan.lua
Core\TooltipScan.lua

# ── Static Data ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Data\ApiManifest.lua
Data\TBCRaces.lua
Data\TBCWeights.lua
Data\TBCProfessions.lua
Data\TBCTalentHit.lua
Data\TBCTalentBuilds.lua
Data\TBCSecondaryRoles.lua
Data\TBCRotations.lua
Data\TBCLevelingRotations.lua
Data\TBCArmor.lua
Data\TBCPvP.lua
Data\PetFoods.lua

# ── Modules: Infrastructure (load first — everything else logs to it) ──
Modules\Infrastructure\ErrorLog.lua

# ── Modules: Character ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
Modules\Character\Character.lua
Modules\Character\StatCaps.lua
Modules\Character\WeaponSkill.lua
Modules\Character\RaceAdvisor.lua
Modules\Character\ProfessionAdvisor.lua
Modules\Character\PetCare.lua
Modules\Character\TalentBuilds.lua
Modules\Character\Rotation.lua
Modules\Character\Spells.lua

# ── Modules: Gear ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Modules\Gear\Gear.lua

# ── Modules: PvP ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Modules\PvP\PvPAdvisor.lua

# Bindings.xml is deliberately NOT listed here. WoW loads an addon's
# Bindings.xml automatically from the addon root; listing it in the TOC makes
# the client parse it a second time as ordinary UI XML, where <Binding> is not
# a valid element -- that is the "Unrecognized XML: Binding" seen on login
# 2026-08-16. Corrected 2026-08-29.
#
# The earlier diagnosis (a `category` attribute on <Binding>) was wrong.
# Census of all 63 addons shipping a Bindings.xml across the five installs:
# 51 of them use category= and load fine, and ToonAge was the only addon in
# any client that listed Bindings.xml in its TOC. That listing was the one
# variable unique to ToonAge.
